# ABP Distributed Caching

## Using Typed Cache
Inject `IDistributedCache<TCacheItem>` for type-safe caching:

```csharp
public class BookService : ITransientDependency
{
    private readonly IDistributedCache<BookCacheItem> _cache;

    public async Task<BookCacheItem> GetAsync(Guid bookId)
    {
        return await _cache.GetOrAddAsync(
            bookId.ToString(),
            async () => await GetBookFromDatabaseAsync(bookId),
            () => new DistributedCacheEntryOptions
            {
                AbsoluteExpiration = DateTimeOffset.Now.AddHours(1)
            }
        );
    }
}
```

## Cache Item Class
```csharp
[CacheName("Books")]
public class BookCacheItem
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public decimal Price { get; set; }
}
```

## Using Custom Key Types
Use `IDistributedCache<TCacheItem, TCacheKey>` for non-string keys:
- Override `ToString()` in custom key classes

## Multi-Tenancy
- Cache keys automatically include tenant ID
- Use `[IgnoreMultiTenancy]` on cache item to share across tenants

## Configuration
```csharp
Configure<AbpDistributedCacheOptions>(options =>
{
    options.KeyPrefix = "MyApp";
    options.HideErrors = true;
});
```

## Batch Operations
Use `GetManyAsync`, `SetManyAsync`, `RemoveManyAsync` for better performance

## Unit of Work Integration
Pass `considerUow: true` to sync cache changes with database transaction
